---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Documentation currency is the single most reliable lever in support: help pages
// refreshed within 30 days deflect roughly 45% of contacts, ones untouched for six
// months deflect about 18%. So this page carries its own review date, in public,
// and that date is a commitment rather than decoration.
const REVIEWED = '2026-09-01';
---

<BaseLayout title="Support — 24K Labs" description="How to get help from 24K Labs: what you can answer yourself for free, what to email about, and what we actually promise.">

  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header__glow"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="page-header__badge">Help</span>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Support</h1>
      <p class="page-header__desc">One person reads every message. Here is what we promise, and what we don't.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="sup-block reveal">
        <h2 class="sup-h2">What we promise</h2>
        <p class="sup-lede">
          24K Labs is a small operation — one person, plus a lot of automation. That shapes what
          we can honestly commit to, so here it is in plain terms instead of buried in a policy.
        </p>
        <div class="sup-grid sup-grid--3">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>A reply within two business days</h3>
            <p>
              Every message gets read by a person. If your problem will take longer than that to
              fix, you'll hear <em>that</em> within two days rather than hearing nothing.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>The next update, not a fix time</h3>
            <p>
              We control when we update you. We don't always control when a thing gets fixed. So
              we commit to the first and stay straight with you about the second.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Your money back if we didn't deliver</h3>
            <p>
              If you paid and got nothing, or got something broken, you get refunded. No argument,
              no form. x402 payments refund to the wallet that paid.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="sup-note">
          <strong>What we don't promise:</strong> 24/7 coverage, a phone line, or a one-hour
          response. We would rather under-promise and answer than post a response time we can't keep.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-block reveal">
        <h2 class="sup-h2">Answer it yourself, free</h2>
        <p class="sup-lede">
          Most of what people ask us is faster to settle with a tool than with an email. These are
          free, need no key, and no account.
        </p>
        <div class="sup-grid sup-grid--3">
          <div class="card">
            <h3><a href="/verify">Is this endpoint alive?</a></h3>
            <p>
              Point <code>/verify</code> at any x402 URL. It knocks the endpoint live and reports
              what actually came back. Works on any service, including ones we don't list.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><a href="/api/directory/search">Is it in the directory?</a></h3>
            <p>
              <code>/api/directory/search?q=</code> searches every curated entry. Free and
              ungated — the whole curated shelf is reachable there without paying us anything.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3><a href="/wall/">Browse the shelves</a></h3>
            <p>
              Every listing, by category, server-rendered so crawlers and agents can read it
              without running JavaScript.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-block reveal">
        <h2 class="sup-h2">Buying the directory</h2>
        <div class="sup-grid sup-grid--2">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Full shelf export — $100</h3>
            <p>
              The complete curated shelf, dated, licensed CC-BY-4.0. It is x402-gated at
              <code>/api/v1/directory/bulk</code> for $100 in USDC on Base. No key, no account —
              the payment is the authentication.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>There is no in-browser checkout yet.</strong> Paying that endpoint today
              takes a wallet and an x402 client. If you want the export and that's a barrier,
              email and we'll sort it out with you directly.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Do I have to pay to read the directory?</h3>
            <p>
              No. Reading is free and we intend to keep it that way. The search API returns every
              curated entry at no cost, and the shelves are public.
            </p>
            <p>
              The $100 buys the packaged, dated export with a license attached — not access to
              something we're otherwise hiding from you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-block reveal">
        <h2 class="sup-h2">Still stuck? Email.</h2>
        <div class="sup-contact">
          <a href="mailto:sean@24klabs.ai" class="sup-email">sean@24klabs.ai</a>
          <p class="sup-lede" style="margin-top: 16px;">
            To get a useful answer on the first reply instead of the third, include whichever of
            these you have:
          </p>
          <ul class="sup-list">
            <li><strong>The URL or endpoint</strong> you were using.</li>
            <li><strong>The transaction hash</strong>, if you paid. Every x402 payment has one, and it settles the question of whether money actually moved.</li>
            <li><strong>What you expected and what you got.</strong> Paste the real response if you have it.</li>
            <li><strong>Roughly when</strong> it happened, with a timezone.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="sup-note" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            Found a bug, or want a listing corrected? An issue on
            <a href="https://github.com/Haustorium12/gold-402" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
            is usually faster than email, and it's public, so the fix is visible to everyone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sup-block reveal">
        <h2 class="sup-h2">Common questions</h2>
        <div class="sup-grid sup-grid--2">

          <div class="card">
            <h3>I paid and got nothing back</h3>
            <p>
              Email with the transaction hash. If the payment settled and we didn't deliver, you
              get refunded to the wallet that paid. If it never settled, the hash shows that too,
              and we'll tell you so plainly.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Something about my listing is wrong</h3>
            <p>
              Tell us and we'll fix it. Corrections are free and always will be. We don't charge
              anyone to be listed, to be corrected, or to be placed differently.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>My service got delisted</h3>
            <p>
              Every listing is knocked on a schedule, and entries that stop answering come off the
              shelf. Operators get warned before that happens rather than finding out afterwards.
              If yours came off and you believe it's answering, send the URL — we'll knock it
              while you watch and show you exactly what came back.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>How do I get listed?</h3>
            <p>
              Open a pull request on
              <a href="https://github.com/Haustorium12/gold-402" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gold-402</a>.
              Listing is free. Your endpoint has to answer a live HTTP 402 probe before it gets
              merged — that's the bar, and we don't invent extra ones.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Is something down?</h3>
            <p>
              <a href="/status">/status</a> knocks on every one of our own surfaces at the moment
              you load it — nothing on it is cached from a build or self-reported. There is no
              uptime percentage and no SLA, because we don't keep the history to compute an honest
              one. For any endpoint that isn't ours, <a href="/verify">/verify</a> gives you the
              same live truth. If we're down, email and say so.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>What happens to my data?</h3>
            <p>
              We don't run accounts, so there isn't much of it. What we do keep is in the
              <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which is short and worth the two minutes.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sup-reviewed">
        This page was last reviewed <strong>{REVIEWED}</strong>.
        A support page nobody has re-read in six months is worse than no support page — it answers
        confidently and wrongly. If something here is out of date, that's a bug. Tell us.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sup-h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .sup-lede {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .sup-block { margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .sup-grid { display: grid; gap: 24px; }
  .sup-grid--3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .sup-grid--2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); max-width: 900px; }
  .sup-grid .card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .sup-grid .card h3 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .sup-grid .card h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .sup-grid .card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .sup-grid .card p + p { margin-top: 12px; }
  .sup-note {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 24px;
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .sup-contact { max-width: 760px; }
  .sup-email {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .sup-email:hover { color: var(--gold-light); }
  .sup-list {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .sup-reviewed {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.88em;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .sup-grid--3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .sup-grid--2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
